process-blocks.m's makers spawned on the machine's GPU: arrays of up to
3.2 MB, from the image's cache of large blocks once an earlier maker has
freed one, and each maker's blocks freed as it ends. The most that one
maker held is the last maker's two large arrays, each rounded up to 4 MiB,
with a few small blocks: nothing is freed before its process ends yet
(docs/INPROGRESS.md, Memory that a GPU process gives back, f3).
REQUIRES: amdgpu-gpu

RUN: merkc -O2 -fprocess-declarations --offload-arch=%offload-arch %libomp-flags %S/process-blocks.m -o %t2
RUN: %gpu-env timeout -k 1 60 %t2 gpu | FileCheck %S/process-blocks.m --match-full-lines --strict-whitespace
RUN: %gpu-env MERK_CHECK_PROCESS_MEMORY=1 MERK_CHECK_DEVICE_MEMORY=1 timeout -k 1 60 %t2 gpu 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --match-full-lines
CHECK:300000: right
CHECK-NEXT:Mercury runtime: 0 chunks of the devices' arenas and 0 rings are allocated
CHECK-NEXT:Mercury runtime: a GPU process held at most {{838[89][0-9][0-9][0-9]}} bytes of blocks at once
